e consistent encoding (they said all sources cp1251... hmm AGENTS says source encoding CP1251; but they later changed many to UTF-8). Actually cmake reads CMakeLists as UTF-8 typically; non-UTF-8 bytes in comments could produce warnings with newer versions. Might note as check. Let me not overclaim.\n\nLet me carefully verify the missing endif & unbalanced-if: lines 46-50:\n```\n  if(NOT args) \n    string(JOIN ... PREFIX ${NATIVE_PATH_MAIN} < ${input})\n  else\n    string(JOIN ... PREFIX ${NATIVE_PATH_MAIN} ${args} < ${input}) \n```\nthen line 52 `string(JOIN ... RUN_MAIN...)`. No endif → unbalanced. That yields config error. Actually wait, maybe intended indentation suggests they thought endif after else at line50 but forgot. Yes.\n\nBut also note argument expansion `PREFIX ${NATIVE_PATH_MAIN} < ${input}` unquoted: `${input}` = `tests/input_data/t1_abc` (no ; so one token). Fine-ish.\n\n`if(NOT args)` with args literally \"NULL\" string (truthy). Actually if(args) tests if variable defined & non-false; \"NULL\" string → true. When they pass NULL as placeholder meaning \"no args\", they'd go else branch wrongly. Also ${args} appended into PREFIX → exe receives literal NULL arg. In make, t1 doesn't take args. And t4 does take radius arg. So placeholder \"NULL\" is definitely wrong; should pass empty string \"\". But if(NOT args) with empty → true branch. Good. Using \"NULL\" string was likely a half-way. That's error.\n\n`${run_case}` and `${check}`: Since target not defined, empty. Even if defined, referencing target name as variable doesn't produce path; you need $<TARGET_FILE:...> in NAME/COMMAND form or full path from RUNTIME_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY.\n\n`add_test(${test_name} ${run_case} ...)`: add_test plain name first = test_name, second = command empty → invalid.\n\n`&` literal - plus `&` inside add_test also CMake might interpret? no.\n\n`${CHECK_MODE}` when mode==... but for mode not 1 or 2, CHECK_MODE undefined → empty. modes 1/2 mapping to contains/equal reverse