t, argv[4]=stderr, argv[5]=\"--\", argv[6]=exe. So argc must be at least 7. Check `argc < 7` correct. And \"--\" at argv[5] checked. Good.\n\nWait: also line 44 argc<7 means minimum argc=7 → argv[6] exists. Good.\n\nNow about the question: \"что с PROCESS_INFORMATION pi{}; line 113? он остаётся пустым?\" — ProcessInfo is out-param; CreateProcess fills hProcess, hThread, dwProcessId, dwThreadId. We zero-init then pass &pi; after successful call it's populated. So it doesn't stay empty — CreateProcess writes into it. Zero init is just safety. So answer her question: it's filled by CreateProcessA on success.\n\nLet me formulate answer with categories and confidence. Also we're in plan mode - cannot edit. So I just review and point out. Provide the fix snippet for expected_code scope.\n\nAlso diagnostics for stoi out_of_range should include the value. Minor 4.6 style note.\n\nAnother potential issue: encoding of messages — irrelevant here.\n\nCheck also: if `in`/`out` opened but later steps fail early, close. Process exits; OS reclaims handles automatically on process termination, so not a real leak in a short-lived test tool. I'll note it but low severity.\n\nAlso one more subtlety: The catch of invalid_argument — but the message prints argv[1]; fine.\n\nAlso line 60: out_of_range message doesn't include received value, per 4.6 should say. Minor.\n\nLet me also double check main() return paths: In #ifdef branch, line 158 return 0; ok. On failure returns 1. Good. #else returns 1. good.\n\nBut note: any `return 1` inside #ifdef between line 77..156 — fine. But line 45/50 returns happen before expected_code declared — fine.\n\nWhat about compiled without _WIN32? includes std::print etc available C++23. ok.\n\nAlso gcc/linux compile: windows.h excluded. SECURITY_ATTRIBUTES etc excluded. GOOD — everything win is inside #ifdef. expected_code moved above — good for both.\n\nNow also there is subtle bug: in the catches, variable name e unused → -Wall may complain about unused parameter? Actually for catch clauses GCC may not warn. MSVC /W4? catch param unused - I don't think warns. But to be safe name removal possible. Not critical.\n\nI'll give review list.\n\nSummary of required fixes:\n1. Critical: expected_code scoping — declare outside try. (compile error C2065)\n2. CreateProcess fills pi — answer question.\n3. Minor: on failure after partial file opens, handles not closed — but process exits, OS cleans; note as accepted for now, or close on error path too.\n4. 4.6 style: out_of_range message lacks received value; also invalid_argument messages maybe wording — but she's fine-ish. Actually rule says: what failed, what value, what allowed. \"Ожидался exit-code - целое число. Получено: argv[1]\" good. For out_of_range should also include argv[1].\n5. unused catch var e - optional.\n6. Cleanup of old commented main / unused includes before commit (already flagged).\n7. Line 44 message: \"Недостаточно аргументов...\" vs \"ожидалось\"? wording fine.\n\nWait also possible warning: `e` in catch unused. minor.\n\nAlso: variables in/out named err shadows? `err` HANDLE at 95 and later `DWORD err = GetLastError();` at 126 in !ok branch — different scopes? DWORD err inside if block, HANDLE err in function scope. Inside `if (!ok)` block, `DWORD err` declared shadows HANDLE err? The `if` body is a nested scope, so `DWORD err` inside hides outer `err`. Not a compile error. But readability meh. At line 137 inside another if, DWORD err again shadows. Not error. Fine but mention? minor; could rename DWORD to last_err. Low priority.\n\nLine 144: GetExitCodeProcess message lacks detail, fine-ish.\n\nLet me answer concisely. In plan mode: only report, propose fixes; no edits. Provide answer.",
